  "notes": "The scene preset for the bedroom-made wave that charted, and its whole identity is that it is *less* than its parent, not darker than it. Four parameters carry that. `session.keys` is authored rather than inherited because the research gives a real, unusual reason for it: F/G/A minor centres are common *because the beats are built around stock piano and bell presets left near their default register* — so `melody.register` drops out of the parent's bell octave into that default range too. `melody.loopVerbatim` and the 5:2 weight on 2-bar phrases encode the documented \"extreme repetition by design\". The 808 is louder and longer than the parent's and glides at most once a bar, so `bass808.sustain` stays legato while `slidesPer4Bars` falls to 1–2. `humanize` is not touched, but `hihat.velocities` are flat-topped because everything is mixed hot enough that the transients smear. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates this high-medium: the aesthetic and one hard anchor (\"Gucci Gang\", 120 BPM in F) are sourced and every other tempo in the 120–155 range is the inferred parameter. ⚠ The 32nd hat bursts the research names are carried by `fillDensity`; the roll vocabulary is held to 16ths at one position so this batch's fills stay distinguishable. ⚠ `arrangement.transitions.switchUpProb` is 0 on purpose — \"no bridge, no beat switch\" is a stated trait, not an omission.",
